1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,433
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,233
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:40,967 --> 00:00:42,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:45,767
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:54,433 --> 00:00:55,533
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:56,933 --> 00:00:58,500
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:58,633 --> 00:00:59,833
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:00:59,967 --> 00:01:01,167
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:02,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:06,300
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,333
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:12,233 --> 00:01:16,067
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:18,333
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:20,700
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:20,833 --> 00:01:23,600
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:27,200
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:29,567 --> 00:01:30,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:33,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:34,433 --> 00:01:35,333
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:35,467 --> 00:01:36,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,100
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:40,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,367 --> 00:01:47,100
<i>It's not easy
to get Ginintuang Lupa.</i>

24
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:49,200
<i> The people there can kill.</i>

25
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:50,567
<i> This is our land!</i>

26
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:51,800
<i> This is where we were born!</i>

27
00:01:51,933 --> 00:01:53,033
<i> And this is where we'll die!</i>

28
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:54,267
<i> We'll fight back!</i>

29
00:01:56,267 --> 00:01:58,433
<i>You know, it's better if you
put the clearing operations</i>

30
00:01:58,567 --> 00:01:59,533
<i> on hold for now.</i>

31
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:00,900
<i> I know what I'm doing</i>

32
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:02,833
<i>and what I should do
with my property!</i>

33
00:02:02,967 --> 00:02:05,667
<i>I will not let anybody
tell me what to do!</i>

34
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,200
<i> Most especially you, Samantha.</i>

35
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:08,400
<i> Start the demolition!</i>

36
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,667
<i> Neighbors! Let's fight back!</i>

37
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,500
<i> We were born in this land,</i>

38
00:02:15,667 --> 00:02:18,367
<i> and we will die in this land!</i>

39
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,733
<i> Keep going!</i>

40
00:02:20,467 --> 00:02:22,333
We are here at Ginintuang Lupa.

41
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:26,467
<i>We're witnessing police
brutality in this community.</i>

42
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:38,367
- [WATER SPLASHING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:38,933 --> 00:02:39,900
[CAR HOOD SQUEAKS]

44
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:45,067
- [BLOWS, KICK LANDING]
- [GRUNTING, GROANING]

45
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,400
[BLOW, KICK LAND]

46
00:02:48,567 --> 00:02:49,600
Come on!

47
00:02:49,733 --> 00:02:50,900
That's what I'm talking about!

48
00:02:51,033 --> 00:02:53,267
You can't take this land
from us! [LAUGHS EVILLY]

49
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,367
Django, Django.

50
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:55,867
Look, it's Gabo.

51
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:57,900
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

52
00:02:58,033 --> 00:02:58,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,700
Great timing!

54
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:01,833
[LAUGHS MANIACALLY]

55
00:03:01,967 --> 00:03:04,233
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

56
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:06,600
Move!

57
00:03:08,467 --> 00:03:09,733
[GUNSHOT]

58
00:03:13,467 --> 00:03:14,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

59
00:03:14,733 --> 00:03:15,667
[BODY THUDS]

60
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,933
[SCREAMS] Rudy!

61
00:03:20,167 --> 00:03:21,400
Rudy!

62
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,167
Rudy!

63
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,367
Pa!

64
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:28,633
Gabo!

65
00:03:29,267 --> 00:03:31,167
I might have failed to kill you,

66
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:33,033
but now we're even!

67
00:03:33,167 --> 00:03:34,067
[LAUGHS EVILLY]

68
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,167
Let's go!

69
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:36,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

70
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:38,733
[BETCHAY WAILING]

71
00:03:38,867 --> 00:03:39,833
Pa!

72
00:03:40,367 --> 00:03:41,367
Help!

73
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,233
- Help! Please help us!
- Somebody help!

74
00:03:43,367 --> 00:03:45,533
- Help! Pa!
- Help us!

75
00:03:45,667 --> 00:03:46,800
Uncle Rudy!

76
00:03:46,933 --> 00:03:48,333
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

77
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:49,467
Let's carry Papa!

78
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:50,833
Hurry! Hurry up!

79
00:03:50,967 --> 00:03:52,533
Let's take him to the hospital!

80
00:03:52,667 --> 00:03:54,767
Help! Please!

81
00:03:54,933 --> 00:03:56,467
- [MEN GRUNTING]
- [WAILING CONTINUES]

82
00:03:58,967 --> 00:04:00,867
Django, what if Gabo
finds out about this?

83
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,133
Then good!

84
00:04:02,267 --> 00:04:05,500
At least he'll know what happens
if he dares cross me again.

85
00:04:13,433 --> 00:04:15,000
I know why you're here.

86
00:04:15,933 --> 00:04:17,133
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

87
00:04:17,267 --> 00:04:18,467
I was in the right.

88
00:04:19,433 --> 00:04:21,267
So we have nothing left
to talk about.

89
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:28,400
Ricardo, I want you
to listen to me.

90
00:04:30,567 --> 00:04:34,567
Every day Sam makes an effort
to be close to you.

91
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:36,033
But you...

92
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:41,533
You always look for a reason
to start a fight with her.

93
00:04:42,067 --> 00:04:43,033
[GLASS THUDS]

94
00:04:43,633 --> 00:04:46,133
That's beside the point, Isobel!

95
00:04:46,267 --> 00:04:47,200
[SIGHS]

96
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:51,767
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

97
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:53,300
Okay, tell me.

98
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,867
I'm here to listen.

99
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:03,667
If it weren't for me
and the way I hustled,

100
00:05:05,233 --> 00:05:07,433
they wouldn't have grown up
living a comfortable life.

101
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:12,067
They have me to thank for
the good life they enjoy now.

102
00:05:15,767 --> 00:05:18,533
I don't want your daughter
lecturing me...

103
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:21,767
as if I were useless!

104
00:05:22,867 --> 00:05:25,033
She wasn't lecturing you.

105
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:28,733
Your daughter was just worried.

106
00:05:28,867 --> 00:05:30,967
She was only giving
a suggestion.

107
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:32,233
That's all.

108
00:05:32,367 --> 00:05:37,133
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

109
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,033
I once made the mistake...

110
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:42,967
of listening to someone
I should've never listened to.

111
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:48,433
That won't happen again, Isobel.

112
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:58,067
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

113
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,033
[ENGINE REVVING]

114
00:06:01,167 --> 00:06:02,867
- Help! We need help!
- Help!

115
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,100
- Guard, help!
- [HORN HONKING]

116
00:06:04,233 --> 00:06:05,867
- Emergency! Emergency!
- Help us!

117
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,900
- [WOMAN] Drop him off here!
- [MAN] Be careful!

118
00:06:08,067 --> 00:06:09,167
We have an emergency!

119
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,267
Hang on, wait!

120
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,400
Wait!

121
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:14,333
- Please, Rudy!
- Uncle Rudy!

122
00:06:14,867 --> 00:06:15,967
Rudy!

123
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:17,933
- Rudy, we're here!
- Uncle Rudy!

124
00:06:18,067 --> 00:06:19,067
Rudy!

125
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,467
- Rudy!
- Help me push!

126
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,900
- Hurry up!
- Rudy!

127
00:06:22,033 --> 00:06:24,167
- Uncle Rudy!
- Uncle Rudy, hang in there!

128
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,200
Hurry up!

129
00:06:25,333 --> 00:06:26,433
You're in the hospital now,
Rudy!

130
00:06:26,567 --> 00:06:27,567
Pa!

131
00:06:28,467 --> 00:06:31,267
- Let us through! Move!
- Hang in there, Rudy!

132
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,767
- Pa! Pa!
- The doctor's here!

133
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,033
- Rudy!
- [DOCTOR] What happened?

134
00:06:34,167 --> 00:06:36,133
- [NURSE] It's a gunshot wound.
- [GABO] Doctor! Doctor!

135
00:06:36,267 --> 00:06:37,567
Doctor, my father was shot!

136
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,500
[DOCTOR] Don't worry,
we'll take care of him.

137
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:41,433
- [BETCHAY] Someone shot him!
- [NURSE] Ma'am...

138
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,400
- Ma'am, sir, please.
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:06:43,533 --> 00:06:45,200
Pa! Pa!

140
00:06:45,333 --> 00:06:48,333
[BETCHAY] Rudy, you're
in the hospital now!

141
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

142
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:07,200
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

143
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,633
[MAN]
Guys, come get your weapons.

144
00:07:11,767 --> 00:07:12,800
[OBJECT THUDS]

145
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:13,933
There's no need for that!

146
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,733
Oh, why?

147
00:07:15,867 --> 00:07:17,400
Is the demolition team
not coming back?

148
00:07:17,533 --> 00:07:18,567
They're gone.

149
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,467
Those bastards already left.

150
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,467
[LAUGHS EVILLY]

151
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,233
That's what I'm talking about!

152
00:07:23,367 --> 00:07:26,633
Good thing they failed
to ruin our homes.

153
00:07:26,767 --> 00:07:28,233
The fun continues!

154
00:07:28,367 --> 00:07:29,700
Back to business as usual!

155
00:07:29,833 --> 00:07:31,167
Money will keep flowing!

156
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:33,733
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

157
00:07:33,867 --> 00:07:37,533
The threat of demolition
is not new to us.

158
00:07:37,667 --> 00:07:38,667
- Right.
- Right.

159
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,700
That's why we need
to keep the cash flow steady!

160
00:07:41,833 --> 00:07:43,300
- Right!
- Right!

161
00:07:43,433 --> 00:07:44,867
Even if this situation
costs lives,

162
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,100
what's important is that
we're still earning.

163
00:07:48,267 --> 00:07:49,600
- Right.
- Right.

164
00:07:49,733 --> 00:07:52,567
We can't let
other syndicates take over.

165
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,833
- Right!
- No one should be slacking!

166
00:07:55,967 --> 00:07:57,800
Go on! Get back to work!

167
00:07:57,933 --> 00:08:00,733
- Come on!
- Let's do this!

168
00:08:00,867 --> 00:08:02,167
Hurry! Get moving!

169
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,900
Quit slacking off! Hurry up!

170
00:08:04,033 --> 00:08:05,367
Reduce the water in that.

171
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

172
00:08:07,033 --> 00:08:08,233
[MAX] Has Colonel arrived?

173
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,367
Sir.

174
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:13,067
At ease, Lieutenant Jacinto.

175
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,700
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

176
00:08:14,833 --> 00:08:16,267
What happened
with the demolition?

177
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,167
The people of Ginintuang Lupa
fought back.

178
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,133
And the press came and meddled.

179
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:23,233
So we had to suspend
the operation.

180
00:08:23,367 --> 00:08:24,467
Thank you, sir.

181
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:28,367
Uh, Max.

182
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:29,800
Don't worry, Max.

183
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,967
We'll do our best
to get Ginintuang Lupa back.

184
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:35,600
We'll make sure your dad's land
will be returned to you.

185
00:08:43,767 --> 00:08:45,067
It was brutal, Lieutenant.

186
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:46,567
A lot of people got hurt.

187
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:48,500
The press will surely
get this out.

188
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:49,800
Don't worry, Estrella.

189
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:51,767
This is an official operation,

190
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:53,500
so we're
on the right side of this.

191
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:55,600
Go change.

192
00:08:56,767 --> 00:08:57,733
Yes, Ma'am.

193
00:09:10,333 --> 00:09:11,667
- Damn it!
- [SLAMS TABLE]

194
00:09:12,467 --> 00:09:13,667
[HUFFS]

195
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:17,033
Those people
won't really back down, huh?

196
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:19,033
This is bad.

197
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:21,300
It'll be all over the news

198
00:09:21,433 --> 00:09:23,200
that we failed
to conduct the demolition.

199
00:09:26,467 --> 00:09:29,267
I'll arrange a stronger force
for this operation.

200
00:09:29,433 --> 00:09:32,067
We will attack
the people of Ginintuang Lupa.

201
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,333
You said it yourself, sir.

202
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:36,967
We can't fail
the General's orders.

203
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:38,400
I know that, Umali.

204
00:09:41,267 --> 00:09:43,400
I'll deal with General Jacinto.

205
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:48,533
What matters is to get the job
done at Ginintuang Lupa.

206
00:09:50,067 --> 00:09:50,933
Copy, sir.

207
00:09:51,067 --> 00:09:55,267
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,367
[MUSIC FADES]

209
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:57,667
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

210
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:00,033
- Oh, Sam.
- Sir.

211
00:10:00,167 --> 00:10:01,300
You're back.

212
00:10:01,467 --> 00:10:02,800
How are your parents?

213
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:05,333
They're good. They're at home.

214
00:10:07,033 --> 00:10:08,067
Have a seat.

215
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:21,200
Are you having problems
with your Dad again?

216
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:28,767
[EXHALES]

217
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,000
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

218
00:10:30,133 --> 00:10:31,467
Oh, Sam.

219
00:10:36,167 --> 00:10:39,067
Be more patient
with your old man.

220
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:42,133
[LAUGHS]

221
00:10:42,267 --> 00:10:45,167
He's still getting used to
his retirement,

222
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,500
and his life
as a civilian.

223
00:10:47,267 --> 00:10:50,000
When he gets irritated,

224
00:10:50,133 --> 00:10:53,300
it's not about you
or because of you.

225
00:10:53,433 --> 00:10:56,100
Maybe he's struggling to see
his sense of purpose.

226
00:10:56,233 --> 00:10:57,400
He lost his routine.

227
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:04,500
As long as they're okay,
then I'd be okay.

228
00:11:04,633 --> 00:11:07,733
Well, it's good to hear...

229
00:11:08,633 --> 00:11:09,667
that you're okay.

230
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:11,800
So now...

231
00:11:12,867 --> 00:11:14,467
Just focus...

232
00:11:15,667 --> 00:11:16,967
on your job.

233
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:19,300
Yes, sir.

234
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,767
Later, we'll hold a briefing
on the case handed to us.

235
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:24,367
Oh, speaking of which,

236
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:27,867
someone wants to sit in
on our briefing later.

237
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:28,900
Who?

238
00:11:29,033 --> 00:11:33,067
The chief of our research
and review division.

239
00:11:33,767 --> 00:11:35,333
Uh, you mean Ma'am Pia?

240
00:11:35,467 --> 00:11:36,333
Yes.

241
00:11:36,467 --> 00:11:41,100
She's excited to see
how NCIA will solve

242
00:11:41,267 --> 00:11:42,500
the case you're handling.

243
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,300
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

244
00:11:47,433 --> 00:11:48,733
Good luck, Sam.

245
00:11:51,833 --> 00:11:52,933
Alright, sir.

246
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:58,833
[EXHALES]

247
00:12:00,233 --> 00:12:07,267
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

248
00:12:14,933 --> 00:12:15,833
[MUSIC FADES]

249
00:12:15,967 --> 00:12:17,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:12:18,033 --> 00:12:19,133
[BINOY] Gabo is here.

251
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,100
- [BONG] Gabo!
- [TEKLA] Gabo.

252
00:12:22,233 --> 00:12:23,567
Who shot my father?

253
00:12:24,533 --> 00:12:26,100
Did anyone see who
shot my father?!

254
00:12:26,233 --> 00:12:27,600
Gabo, we don't know.

255
00:12:27,733 --> 00:12:28,833
Who else would it be?

256
00:12:28,967 --> 00:12:30,867
Only the cops
carried guns back there.

257
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
I'm sure the bullet that hit
your dad came from them, Gabo.

258
00:12:35,367 --> 00:12:37,100
If something bad happens
to Papa,

259
00:12:37,933 --> 00:12:40,233
I wouldn't think twice
about getting in jail again!

260
00:12:40,367 --> 00:12:43,233
We should direct our anger
to the people

261
00:12:43,367 --> 00:12:45,333
who ordered the cops
to demolish our houses.

262
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:46,833
Tekla is right, Gabo.

263
00:12:46,967 --> 00:12:48,867
The cops were just
following orders.

264
00:12:49,033 --> 00:12:52,067
We should make those landlords
who did this pay!

265
00:12:54,033 --> 00:12:56,333
Let's pray nothing
bad happens to Papa.

266
00:12:57,433 --> 00:13:00,967
If I found out
who ordered that demolition,

267
00:13:01,767 --> 00:13:03,267
I'll make that person pay!

268
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,733
Including their family!

269
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:06,967
[MUSIC TURNS SOMBER]

270
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:10,033
Ginintuang Lupa is at peace,
and now they'd do this?

271
00:13:10,167 --> 00:13:12,367
Mister Rudy isn't the only one
whose life got in danger.

272
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,400
Many of our neighbors
also got hurt.

273
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:18,833
Just say the word, Gabo.
We'll get back at them.

274
00:13:18,967 --> 00:13:20,233
Stop it!

275
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,733
Quit being a thug!

276
00:13:24,467 --> 00:13:26,733
Just think about your father!

277
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:28,333
[MAMENG] Listen to us, Gabo.

278
00:13:28,467 --> 00:13:30,467
Your dad will be okay.

279
00:13:31,467 --> 00:13:32,700
He's strong.

280
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,333
I know he'll be safe.

281
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:44,867
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

282
00:13:57,033 --> 00:13:58,100
Doctor!

283
00:13:58,233 --> 00:14:00,667
- Good day, Doctor.
- How is the patient doing?

284
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:03,733
His vital signs are stable
for now.

285
00:14:03,867 --> 00:14:06,967
But we need to operate
on him right away.

286
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:10,400
There are some supplies and
meds we still have to buy first.

287
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:12,967
Just so you know,
they cost quite a bit.

288
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:15,100
Bring them back here as
soon as you've bought them,

289
00:14:15,233 --> 00:14:17,667
so we can do the surgery
without any more delay.

290
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:20,233
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you, Doctor.

291
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,467
Medicine...

292
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:26,167
We don't have any on hand?
We don't have anything saved up?

293
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:27,533
What are we going to do?

294
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:32,133
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

295
00:14:32,267 --> 00:14:33,367
[SOBS SOFTLY]

296
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:36,700
Um...

297
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:40,900
We don't have anyone
we can turn to, do we?

298
00:14:41,033 --> 00:14:45,267
[BREATH SHAKING]

299
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:50,033
Being this poor is just so hard!

300
00:14:50,167 --> 00:14:53,533
You've got nowhere to lean
on when you need it most!

301
00:14:53,667 --> 00:14:57,867
- [SOBBING]
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

302
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:02,033
Gabo, don't you know
anyone who might help us out?

303
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:07,033
Someone who could lend us money
to save your father's life?

304
00:15:07,167 --> 00:15:08,300
[BETCHAY SOBS SOFTLY]

305
00:15:08,433 --> 00:15:15,400
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

306
00:15:29,167 --> 00:15:30,667
Don't you worry
about any of this.

307
00:15:32,033 --> 00:15:33,733
I'll take care of everything.

308
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:37,533
I'll do whatever it takes
to save Papa.

309
00:15:37,700 --> 00:15:41,333
[SNIFFLING]

310
00:15:41,467 --> 00:15:42,500
[TEKLA] Gabo!

311
00:15:45,167 --> 00:15:52,133
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

312
00:15:53,967 --> 00:15:55,333
Gabo, wait a second.

313
00:15:57,433 --> 00:15:58,967
Gabo, where are you going?

314
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:03,667
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

315
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,633
I need to find some money

316
00:16:05,767 --> 00:16:07,267
to buy the medicine
Papa needs.

317
00:16:08,967 --> 00:16:12,200
Where are you supposed to find
that kind of money right now?

318
00:16:12,333 --> 00:16:13,400
[TOLITS]
I've got an idea.

319
00:16:14,467 --> 00:16:15,500
Gabo.

320
00:16:15,633 --> 00:16:18,533
Let's rob a pawnshop,
a bus, or even a bank

321
00:16:18,667 --> 00:16:22,033
to get the cash we need
for Mister Rudy's medicine.

322
00:16:22,167 --> 00:16:23,667
I know a place.
It's an easy target.

323
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:25,433
- So, are you in?
- No way.

324
00:16:28,267 --> 00:16:32,200
We won't do anything
wrong just to save Papa's life.

325
00:16:33,467 --> 00:16:35,567
Gabo, what are we
supposed to do now?

326
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:36,633
[BONG] Yeah.

327
00:16:36,767 --> 00:16:38,500
We really don't have
anyone else to turn to,

328
00:16:38,633 --> 00:16:39,867
especially not
anyone around here.

329
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,633
If we tried borrowing
from Mister Paquito,

330
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:44,733
he'd never lend us a
cent, he hates our guts.

331
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:53,433
I know how we can
get the money we need.

332
00:16:53,567 --> 00:17:00,600
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

333
00:17:03,533 --> 00:17:05,367
Ricardo, please...

334
00:17:05,500 --> 00:17:07,600
I don't ever want to go
back to that place again.

335
00:17:07,733 --> 00:17:11,100
Even now, I still
feel dirty all over,

336
00:17:11,233 --> 00:17:13,433
smelling like mud and grime.

337
00:17:13,567 --> 00:17:14,667
Huh? Please?

338
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,600
We have to go
back there, Isobel.

339
00:17:16,767 --> 00:17:19,033
After all, we already
bought Ginintuang Lupa.

340
00:17:19,167 --> 00:17:21,667
[REPORTER ON TV]<i> The
</i> demolition at Ginintuang Lupa

341
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:22,900
<i> turned violent earlier today.</i>

342
00:17:23,033 --> 00:17:25,033
<i>Here's the report
from Salvador Manalo.</i>

343
00:17:25,167 --> 00:17:28,333
[SALVADOR] We are
here at Ginintuang Lupa!

344
00:17:28,467 --> 00:17:34,933
<i>What was supposed to be
a calm, peaceful demolition</i>

345
00:17:35,067 --> 00:17:38,500
<i>erupted into chaos
when shots were fired!</i>

346
00:17:38,633 --> 00:17:40,533
<i>We won't stop
covering this story!</i>

347
00:17:40,667 --> 00:17:43,767
<i>We will get to the bottom
of what caused this violence.</i>

348
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:48,400
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [OBJECTS CLATTERING ON TV]

349
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:49,900
Oh my god!

350
00:17:51,333 --> 00:17:52,533
Ricardo, the...

351
00:17:52,667 --> 00:17:55,600
Ginintuang Lupa
is all over the news!

352
00:17:55,733 --> 00:17:57,567
They brought this on themselves.

353
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,933
Oh my god, no!

354
00:18:00,067 --> 00:18:01,833
That's a bad publicity for us.

355
00:18:01,967 --> 00:18:04,567
We can't let this drag us in.

356
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:07,700
Then you better fix this mess
and protect our reputation.

357
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:09,533
But as far as I'm concerned,

358
00:18:09,667 --> 00:18:12,067
I won't stop until every
last one of them is gone.

359
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:19,167
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:34,633
[LINE RINGING]

361
00:18:34,767 --> 00:18:35,900
Colonel.

362
00:18:36,033 --> 00:18:37,533
General Jacinto.

363
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:39,300
I thought we had an agreement?

364
00:18:39,433 --> 00:18:41,967
The people at Ginintuang
Lupa fought back.

365
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:44,667
Many were hurt, many were shot.

366
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:47,733
That's why we had
to pull out.

367
00:18:47,867 --> 00:18:49,167
That's exactly what I hate most.

368
00:18:50,367 --> 00:18:54,033
You botched the job, and
now you make excuses.

369
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:56,133
<i> Fix this immediately.</i>

370
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:59,233
Make sure no one traces
the shooting back to you.

371
00:18:59,367 --> 00:19:02,133
My lawyer and I will handle
getting them removed.

372
00:19:02,267 --> 00:19:03,900
Copy that, General Jacinto.

373
00:19:04,033 --> 00:19:11,000
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

374
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:25,033
[INDISTINCT BACKGROUND CHATTER]

375
00:19:25,167 --> 00:19:26,167
Hey!

376
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:28,067
Why do you keep following us?

377
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,167
Yeah.

378
00:19:29,333 --> 00:19:31,367
You wouldn't let us be,
even at the hospital.

379
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:33,167
Didn't we tell you?

380
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:35,200
We want to be part
of your group!

381
00:19:35,333 --> 00:19:36,467
And we already told you no!

382
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:37,600
So, scram!

383
00:19:38,567 --> 00:19:39,467
Go!

384
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:41,233
We just want to join your group.

385
00:19:41,367 --> 00:19:44,933
And we promise we'll be good.

386
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:46,600
[TEKLA SCOFFS]

387
00:19:46,733 --> 00:19:47,733
Gabo.

388
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,267
Do we have to take
these three along?

389
00:19:53,267 --> 00:19:54,733
- Hey, whoa!
- You three!

390
00:19:54,867 --> 00:19:56,033
You'd better behave!

391
00:19:56,167 --> 00:19:58,700
Don't you dare make a mess
and get us involved!

392
00:19:58,833 --> 00:20:00,067
We don't want any trouble!

393
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:02,867
No, no. We won't do
anything stupid, promise.

394
00:20:03,033 --> 00:20:04,267
Also...

395
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:05,667
We want to help Gabo

396
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:07,300
so Uncle Rudy can have
his operation.

397
00:20:07,433 --> 00:20:09,567
- Yeah, that's right.
- Don't mess with us.

398
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:10,867
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

399
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,667
So, what's the plan, Gabo?

400
00:20:18,100 --> 00:20:19,400
- Hey, you three!
- We know!

401
00:20:19,533 --> 00:20:20,633
Enough with the threats!

402
00:20:20,767 --> 00:20:21,800
[DOCTOR] Ma'am, as of now,

403
00:20:21,933 --> 00:20:24,833
Mr. Magtibay's condition is
still not good.

404
00:20:24,967 --> 00:20:27,400
He needs to be transferred
to the ICU

405
00:20:27,533 --> 00:20:29,933
so we can keep track
of his vital signs

406
00:20:30,067 --> 00:20:31,733
and overall health.

407
00:20:31,867 --> 00:20:32,900
Okay?

408
00:20:34,433 --> 00:20:36,200
We need to arrange
his transfer now.

409
00:20:36,367 --> 00:20:37,633
- Thank you.
- Alright, then.

410
00:20:38,967 --> 00:20:40,033
ICU...

411
00:20:40,633 --> 00:20:41,833
ICU?

412
00:20:42,767 --> 00:20:44,900
Another expense again.

413
00:20:45,633 --> 00:20:48,233
Where will Gabo get the money?

414
00:20:48,367 --> 00:20:51,133
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

415
00:20:51,267 --> 00:20:52,800
What do you think?

416
00:20:54,333 --> 00:20:58,800
Since we're desperate for money,
where will he get it?

417
00:20:58,933 --> 00:21:01,133
From the only work he knows.

418
00:21:01,267 --> 00:21:02,733
I hope I'm wrong, but...

419
00:21:02,867 --> 00:21:05,000
I think that's where
he'll end up again.

420
00:21:05,533 --> 00:21:06,800
You know what, Betchay?

421
00:21:07,333 --> 00:21:09,700
Just when will you get off
Gabo's back, huh?

422
00:21:10,267 --> 00:21:11,267
You're too harsh!

423
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,233
I'm not harsh!

424
00:21:14,167 --> 00:21:15,067
I'm just being honest!

425
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:17,233
Let's be real!

426
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:19,533
What are you implying?

427
00:21:20,733 --> 00:21:22,700
That he'll do something
illegal again?

428
00:21:22,833 --> 00:21:24,367
Isn't it possible?

429
00:21:24,933 --> 00:21:26,800
Couldn't it happen?

430
00:21:26,933 --> 00:21:28,533
Gabo won't do that,

431
00:21:28,667 --> 00:21:31,533
because he knows
Rudy will be furious

432
00:21:31,667 --> 00:21:33,600
if he finds out the money
for his treatment came

433
00:21:33,733 --> 00:21:35,000
from an illegal source.

434
00:21:35,133 --> 00:21:36,300
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

435
00:21:36,433 --> 00:21:37,867
I hope you're right.

436
00:21:45,433 --> 00:21:46,833
- [WATER SPLASHING]
- [HORN HONKING]

437
00:21:49,233 --> 00:21:52,100
[GABO] I need a huge amount
of money for Papa's operation.

438
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:54,133
Look, Gabo....

439
00:21:54,267 --> 00:21:56,067
Are we really going to do this?

440
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:57,733
It's embarrassing!

441
00:21:57,867 --> 00:22:00,400
We're all grown and hefty,
and still begging?

442
00:22:00,533 --> 00:22:01,567
What choice do we have?

443
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:03,633
Gabo needs the money, remember?

444
00:22:03,767 --> 00:22:05,767
There are lots of options
out there.

445
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:07,400
You want us to mug someone?

446
00:22:07,533 --> 00:22:09,233
- Or snatch stuff?
- Yeah.

447
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:11,467
[BETCHAY]
We want to help Gabo, right?

448
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:14,067
So how about we just listen
to what he says?

449
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:18,333
We won't commit crimes
just to help my father.

450
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:20,467
If we have to beg,

451
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,167
we will.

452
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:24,300
As long as my father
gets his surgery.

453
00:22:24,433 --> 00:22:28,167
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

454
00:22:28,300 --> 00:22:32,167
[ECG MACHINE BEEPING]

455
00:22:35,867 --> 00:22:36,800
[DABOY] Please, we need help.

456
00:22:36,933 --> 00:22:38,467
My friend's father is
in the hospital. Shot.

457
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:39,967
[GABO] Miss, just a
little help, please.

458
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:41,433
[TEKLA] Sir, maybe you can
spare something.

459
00:22:41,567 --> 00:22:42,533
Any amount at all.

460
00:22:42,667 --> 00:22:43,800
Geez, get a job!

461
00:22:43,933 --> 00:22:45,367
That's why nothing changes
in the Philippines!

462
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:46,833
You people rely on handouts!

463
00:22:46,967 --> 00:22:49,367
You've got such a big body.
Why don't you look for work?

464
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:51,533
For all we know,
you might just rob us!

465
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:52,600
Let's go!

466
00:22:52,733 --> 00:22:54,100
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

467
00:22:54,233 --> 00:22:55,300
You're so arrogant!

468
00:22:55,433 --> 00:22:57,067
I look richer than you!

469
00:22:57,200 --> 00:22:58,767
Come with me instead.
What do you say?

470
00:22:58,900 --> 00:22:59,800
Are you serious?!

471
00:22:59,933 --> 00:23:01,667
I'm only asking for help
for my friend!

472
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:02,900
I'm not that kind of girl!

473
00:23:03,033 --> 00:23:05,167
Shame on you! You even came
from church! Just go!

474
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,833
Any amount will do, please.

475
00:23:08,667 --> 00:23:15,633
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

476
00:23:16,933 --> 00:23:22,700
[BEEPING CONTINUES]

477
00:23:32,767 --> 00:23:34,067
- Gabo, don't worry.

478
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:36,400
<i>Everything we earn,
we'll give to you</i>

479
00:23:36,533 --> 00:23:38,233
<i>so Uncle Rudy can have
his operation.</i>

480
00:23:38,367 --> 00:23:40,133
<i>Let's think of another way
to help Gabo.</i>

481
00:23:40,267 --> 00:23:42,633
<i>I know something. I'm sure
we'll earn big from this!</i>

482
00:23:42,767 --> 00:23:43,800
<i>- Where?
- Huh?</i>

483
00:23:44,467 --> 00:23:46,333
<i>S-So what kind of job
will we have there?</i>

484
00:23:46,467 --> 00:23:47,700
<i> Male strippers!</i>

485
00:23:47,833 --> 00:23:51,133
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [WHISTLING, CHEERING]

486
00:23:51,267 --> 00:23:53,233
<i>Bring the boys in.
It's time to pick.</i>

487
00:23:53,367 --> 00:23:54,400
<i> Here we go!</i>

488
00:23:55,367 --> 00:23:59,133
<i> I'll take good care of you.</i>

489
00:23:59,267 --> 00:24:00,367
- [BONES CRACKING]
- [EXCLAIMS]

490
00:24:00,500 --> 00:24:02,300
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [ALL CLAMORING]

491
00:24:02,433 --> 00:24:03,733
<i>- What?!
- Helping him is pointless.</i>

492
00:24:03,867 --> 00:24:05,367
<i>We show concern,
but we're still blamed.</i>

493
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:06,600
<i> Did I ask for your help?</i>

494
00:24:06,733 --> 00:24:08,433
<i>I don't need any of you!
I can manage!</i>

495
00:24:08,567 --> 00:24:11,500
<i>Why can't you just try
to understand him?!</i>

496
00:24:11,633 --> 00:24:14,533
<i>That Gabo didn't just
beat up Django.</i>

497
00:24:14,667 --> 00:24:16,433
<i> He ruined our businesses, too!</i>

498
00:24:16,567 --> 00:24:18,000
<i> Prepare our men.</i>

499
00:24:18,133 --> 00:24:20,533
Tonight, we're taking Gabo down.

500
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:25,267
<i>Who are you?
What do you want from me?!</i>

501
00:24:25,867 --> 00:24:27,967
- [THWACKS]
- [KICKS LANDING]

502
00:24:30,300 --> 00:24:31,300
[GUNSHOT]
